    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21975" root="شذب" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَجُلٌ شَذِبُ العُرُوقِ</span></b>  (assumed tropical:)  <i>A man whose veins are
apparent.</i> (S, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شذب</span> [app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَذِبٌ</span>] is
syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَظِبٌ</span>, meaning A man <i>alighting,</i> or
<i>abiding, in places of dried-up herbage, and in a
waterless desert.</i> (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عظب</span>.)

